. The Precision Medicine and Manufacturing segment designs, manufactures, and markets laser beam steering and scanning solutions, laser sources, robotic and precision motion, robotic end-of-arm tooling, and bearing spindles. This segment serves advanced industrial processes, advanced industrial and medical robotics, other medical and life science automation applications, and medical laser procedures, such as ophthalmology applications. The Medical Solutions segment provides a range of medical grade technologies, including medical insufflators, pumps, and related disposables; imaging, identification and RFID solutions; advanced motion control solutions; and light engines, and integrated operating room technologies. The company was formerly known as GSI Group, Inc. and changed its name to Novanta Inc. in May 2016. Novanta Inc. was incorporated in 1968 and is based in Bedford, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthijs  Glastra | CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $327K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $16K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Novanta Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $4.5B market cap on $981M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 42%.","The business throws off $48M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.19\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 4.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.9%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 427% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":4.2746172096685955},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $7.1M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-7129279.18},{"text":"Significant goodwill (36% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 9% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(NOVT) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/101/NOVT_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_111226055401_1794524041.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794524041.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Novanta (NASDAQ:NOVT) Issues Quarterly Earnings Results, Beats Estimates By $0.08 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/novanta-nasdaqnovt-issues-quarterly-earnings-results-beats-estimates-by-0-08-eps.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794409029.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","legal"]},{"title":"Novanta (NASDAQ:NOVT) Issues FY 2026 Earnings Guidance","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/novanta-nasdaqnovt-issues-fy-2026-earnings-guidance.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794400894.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance","legal"]},{"title":"Novanta (NOVT) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/novanta-novt-q3-2026-earnings-233050000.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794353789.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Novanta outlines 2027 outlook of more than 15% reported growth as it works t